    "identifiable model class",
    "mu_1 > mu_2"
   ],
   "tuning": [],
   "is_new": true,
   "source": {
    "label": "thm:2arms",
    "number": "Theorem (thm:2arms)",
    "quote": "Let $\\mathbf{\\nu}=(\\nu_{1},\\nu_{2})$ be a two-armed bandit model such that $\\mu_1>\\mu_2$. In the fixed-budget setting, any consistent algorithm satisfies \\[ \\limsup_{t\\rightarrow \\infty}-\\frac{1}{t} \\log p_t(\\nu) \\leq c^*(\\nu),\\ \\ \\ \\text{where} \\ \\ \\ c^*(\\nu) := \\inf_{(\\nu_1',\\nu_2')\\in\\cM: \\mu'_1 <\\mu'_2} \\max\\left\\{\\K(\\nu_1',\\nu_{1}),\\K(\\nu_2',\\nu_{2})\\right\\}. \\]"
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Statement is on the error exponent; encoded as p_T >= exp(-(c_star+o(1))T). Implies kappa_B >= 1/c^*. For Gaussian known variances c^* = (mu1-mu2)^2/(2(sigma1+sigma2)^2)."
  },
